  "plan": {
    "summary": "BRO-5521: twelve capitalizations were 4 x the show’s NY tax credit (credit / 25%). The 25% applies to qualified production and running costs, so 4 x overstates: the SEC Form Ds found under the tax-credit recipients’ entity names put nine of these shows at 1.7x to 3.6x their credit (median 2.6). Nine get their filed figure with the filing cited (Hangmen stays an estimate: its 2019 filing predates the pandemic delay). Death of a Salesman (2022), Peter Pan Goes Wrong and Plaza Suite have no usable filing (Plaza Suite’s Suite 719 LLC filing says \"Indefinite\") and are re-estimated at 2.6 x credit with the range stated. Model rerun on apply; no designation conflicts (flops stay negative; Macbeth 52% -> 87%, Good Night Oscar 26% -> 40% central). (part 1 of 2: topdog-underdog-2022, macbeth-2022, potus-or-behind-every-great-dumbass-are-seven-women-trying-to-keep-him-alive-2022, the-minutes-2022, hangmen-2022)",
    "steps": [
      "Filed figures: capitalization, a Form D citation, the estimate flag, and the filing in sources; notes that repeated the 4 x figure are corrected.",
      "Re-estimates: capitalization at 2.6 x credit (rounded to $0.1M) with the method and range in capitalizationSource."
    ],
